{
  "Dockerfile": "- **File Path**: `Dockerfile`\n- **High-Level Purpose**: Defines the instructions for building a Docker image for the Go application, utilizing a multi-stage build process for an optimized final image.\n- **Definitions in the File**:\n    - **Build Stage (`builder`)**:\n        - Base Image: `golang:1.21-alpine`\n        - Working Directory: `/app`\n        - Copies `go.mod` and `go.sum`, downloads Go modules.\n        - Copies the entire project source code.\n        - Builds the Go server binary, disabling CGO and targeting Linux.\n    - **Final Stage**:\n        - Base Image: `alpine:latest`\n        - Working Directory: `/app`\n        - Copies the compiled server binary from the `builder` stage.\n        - Copies the `config.yaml` file.\n        - Exposes port `8080`.\n        - Defines the command to run the server binary when the container starts.\n",
  "Makefile": "- **File Path**: `Makefile`\n- **High-Level Purpose**: Provides a set of convenient commands (targets) for common development and deployment tasks, such as running the application, building binaries, and managing Docker containers.\n- **Definitions in the File**:\n    - **Targets**:\n        - `run`: (PHONY) Executes the Go server directly using `go run`.\n        - `build`: (PHONY) Compiles the Go server binary and places it in `./bin/server`.\n        - `docker-build`: (PHONY) Builds the Docker image for the application.\n        - `docker-up`: (PHONY) Starts the Docker containers defined in `docker-compose.yaml` in detached mode.\n        - `docker-down`: (PHONY) Stops and removes the Docker containers defined in `docker-compose.yaml`.\n",
  "cmd/server/main.go": "- **File Path**: `cmd/server/main.go`\n- **High-Level Purpose**: The main entry point of the application. It initializes the entire application stack, including configuration loading, Redis connection, dependency injection for repositories and usecases, HTTP server setup, a background cleanup job, and graceful shutdown handling.\n- **Definitions in the File**:\n    - **Functions / Methods**:\n        - `main()`: (Public) The application's entry point.\n            - Loads configuration from `config.yaml` and overrides with environment variables.\n            - Initializes and pings the Redis client.\n            - Creates `RedisUserRepository` and `UserUsecase` instances, injecting dependencies.\n            - Starts a background goroutine that periodically calls `userUsecase.CleanupInactiveUsers`.\n            - Initializes the HTTP handlers and router.\n            - Starts the HTTP server on the configured port.\n            - Implements graceful shutdown logic, listening for `SIGINT` and `SIGTERM` signals to shut down the server cleanly.\n- **Notable Patterns or Logic**:\n    - Application entry point.\n    - Manual dependency injection.\n    - Background worker/job for periodic tasks.\n    - Graceful shutdown mechanism for the HTTP server.\n",
  "configs/config.yaml": "- **File Path**: `configs/config.yaml`\n- **High-Level Purpose**: Configuration file for the application, specifying server port, Redis connection details, and application-specific timeouts.\n- **Definitions in the File**:\n    - **Variables / Constants**:\n        - `server.port`: (String) The network address and port for the HTTP server (e.g., \":8080\").\n        - `redis.addr`: (String) The address of the Redis server (e.g., \"localhost:6379\").\n        - `redis.password`: (String) The password for Redis authentication (can be empty).\n        - `redis.db`: (Integer) The Redis database number to use.\n        - `app.user_inactive_timeout_minutes`: (Integer) The duration in minutes after which a user is considered inactive.\n        - `app.username_cooldown_minutes`: (Integer) The duration in minutes for which a username is on cooldown after being released.\n",
  "docker-compose.yaml": "- **File Path**: `docker-compose.yaml`\n- **High-Level Purpose**: Defines and configures a multi-container Docker application, setting up a Redis service and the main application service for local development or deployment.\n- **Definitions in the File**:\n    - **Services**:\n        - `redis`:\n            - Image: `redis:alpine`\n            - Ports: Maps host port 6379 to container port 6379.\n            - Volumes: Mounts a named volume `redis_data` for data persistence.\n        - `app`:\n            - Build: Builds from the local `Dockerfile`.\n            - Ports: Maps host port 8080 to container port 8080.\n            - Depends On: `redis` (ensures Redis starts before the app).\n            - Environment Variables: `REDIS_ADDR` (set to `redis:6379` for inter-container communication), `SERVER_PORT` (set to `:8080`).\n    - **Volumes**:\n        - `redis_data`: A named volume used by the `redis` service.\n",
  "go.mod": "- **File Path**: `go.mod`\n- **High-Level Purpose**: Defines the Go module path and lists all direct and indirect external dependencies required by the `sse-chat` project, along with the Go version.\n- **Definitions in the File**:\n    - **Variables / Constants**:\n        - `module`: `sse-chat` (Module path)\n        - `go`: `1.21` (Required Go version)\n        - `require`: (List of direct dependencies)\n            - `github.com/go-chi/chi/v5 v5.0.12`\n            - `github.com/go-redis/redis/v8 v8.11.5`\n            - `github.com/google/uuid v1.6.0`\n            - `gopkg.in/yaml.v2 v2.4.0`\n        - `require` (indirect): (List of indirect dependencies)\n            - `github.com/cespare/xxhash/v2 v2.1.2`\n            - `github.com/dgryski/go-rendezvous v0.0.0-20200823014737-9f7001d12a5f`\n            - `github.com/onsi/ginkgo v1.16.5`\n            - `github.com/onsi/gomega v1.17.0`\n",
  "internal/config/config.go": "- **File Path**: `internal/config/config.go`\n- **High-Level Purpose**: Defines the application's configuration structure and provides a utility function to load these settings from a YAML file.\n- **Definitions in the File**:\n    - **Classes / Structs / Interfaces**:\n        - `Config`: (Public struct) The top-level configuration structure for the application.\n            - Nested Struct `Server`:\n                - Fields: `Port` (string, YAML tag `port`).\n            - Nested Struct `Redis`:\n                - Fields: `Addr` (string, YAML tag `addr`), `Password` (string, YAML tag `password`), `DB` (int, YAML tag `db`).\n            - Nested Struct `App`:\n                - Fields: `UserInactiveTimeout` (time.Duration, YAML tag `user_inactive_timeout_minutes`), `UsernameCooldown` (time.Duration, YAML tag `username_cooldown_minutes`).\n    - **Functions / Methods**:\n        - `LoadConfig(path string) (*Config, error)`: (Public) Reads a YAML file from the given path, unmarshals its content into a `Config` struct, and converts the `user_inactive_timeout_minutes` and `username_cooldown_minutes` fields from integer minutes to `time.Duration`.\n- **Notable Patterns or Logic**:\n    - Configuration management using YAML.\n    - Custom unmarshaling logic for `time.Duration` from integer minutes.",
  "internal/domain/event.go": "- **File Path**: `internal/domain/event.go`\n- **High-Level Purpose**: Defines the `Event` data structure and various `EventType` constants, which are used to represent different occurrences or messages within the chat system, likely for Server-Sent Events (SSE).\n- **Definitions in the File**:\n    - **Classes / Structs / Interfaces**:\n        - `EventType`: (Public type) A string alias used to categorize different types of events.\n    - **Variables / Constants**:\n        - `UserJoined`: (Public, EventType) Constant for a user joining event.\n        - `UserLeft`: (Public, EventType) Constant for a user leaving event.\n        - `UsernameChanged`: (Public, EventType) Constant for a username change event.\n        - `Message`: (Public, EventType) Constant for a chat message event.\n        - `TypingStart`: (Public, EventType) Constant for a user starting to type event.\n        - `TypingStop`: (Public, EventType) Constant for a user stopping typing event.\n        - `Heartbeat`: (Public, EventType) Constant for a heartbeat event.\n        - `Event`: (Public struct) Represents a generic event in the system.\n            - Fields: `EventID` (string), `Timestamp` (time.Time), `Type` (EventType), `FromUserID` (string, optional), `ToUserID` (string, optional), `Payload` (map[string]interface{}).\n",
  "internal/domain/user.go": "- **File Path**: `internal/domain/user.go`\n- **High-Level Purpose**: Defines the `User` data structure, representing the core user entity within the application's domain.\n- **Definitions in the File**:\n    - **Classes / Structs / Interfaces**:\n        - `User`: (Public struct) Represents a user in the chat system.\n            - Fields: `UserID` (string, JSON tag `userId`), `Username` (string, JSON tag `username`), `LastActive` (time.Time, JSON ignored), `IsOnline` (bool, JSON tag `isOnline`), `LastDeliveredEventID` (string, JSON ignored).\n",
  "internal/repository/redis_user_repository.go": "- **File Path**: `internal/repository/redis_user_repository.go`\n- **High-Level Purpose**: Implements the `UserRepository` interface using Redis as the underlying data store. It handles the persistence, retrieval, and management of user data in Redis.\n- **Definitions in the File**:\n    - **Variables / Constants**:\n        - `activeUsersKey`: (Module-level, `string`) Redis key for the sorted set storing active user IDs and their last active timestamps.\n        - `usernamesKey`: (Module-level, `string`) Redis key for the set storing all currently used usernames.\n    - **Functions / Methods**:\n        - `userKey(userID string) string`: (Internal) Helper function to generate the Redis key for a specific user's data.\n        - `usernameCooldownKey(username string) string`: (Internal) Helper function to generate the Redis key for a username's cooldown status.\n    - **Classes / Structs / Interfaces**:\n        - `redisUserRepository`: (Private struct) Implements the `UserRepository` interface.\n            - Fields: `client` (*redis.Client).\n    - **Functions / Methods**:\n        - `NewRedisUserRepository(client *redis.Client) *redisUserRepository`: (Public) Constructor function that creates and returns a new `redisUserRepository` instance.\n        - `(r *redisUserRepository) Create(ctx context.Context, user *domain.User) error`: (Public method) Stores a new user's data in Redis, adds their ID to the `activeUsersKey` sorted set, and their username to the `usernamesKey` set, using a Redis transaction pipeline.\n        - `(r *redisUserRepository) FindByID(ctx context.Context, userID string) (*domain.User, error)`: (Public method) Retrieves a user's data from Redis by their `userID`.\n        - `(r *redisUserRepository) Update(ctx context.Context, user *domain.User) error`: (Public method) Updates an existing user's data in Redis, including their last active timestamp in the sorted set and ensuring their username is in the set, using a Redis transaction pipeline.\n        - `(r *redisUserRepository) Delete(ctx context.Context, userID string) error`: (Public method) Deletes a user's data from Redis, removing them from the `activeUsersKey` sorted set and `usernamesKey` set, using a Redis transaction pipeline.\n        - `(r *redisUserRepository) GetActiveUsers(ctx context.Context) ([]*domain.User, error)`: (Public method) Retrieves all active users by fetching IDs from the `activeUsersKey` sorted set and then fetching individual user data.\n        - `(r *redisUserRepository) FindInactiveUsers(ctx context.Context, timeout time.Duration) ([]string, error)`: (Public method) Finds user IDs in the `activeUsersKey` sorted set whose `LastActive` timestamp is older than the specified timeout.\n        - `(r *redisUserRepository) IsUsernameTaken(ctx context.Context, username string) (bool, error)`: (Public method) Checks if a given username exists in the `usernamesKey` set.\n        - `(r *redisUserRepository) ReleaseUsername(ctx context.Context, username string, cooldown time.Duration) error`: (Public method) Removes a username from the `usernamesKey` set and sets a temporary key to put the username on cooldown.\n        - `(r *redisUserRepository) IsUsernameOnCooldown(ctx context.Context, username string) (bool, error)`: (Public method) Checks if a given username is currently on cooldown by checking for the existence of its cooldown key.\n- **Notable Patterns or Logic**:\n    - Repository pattern implementation for user data.\n    - Uses Redis sorted sets for active users (allowing range queries by timestamp) and sets for unique usernames.\n    - Employs Redis pipelines for atomic multi-command operations.\n",
  "internal/transport/http/handler.go": "- **File Path**: `internal/transport/http/handler.go`\n- **High-Level Purpose**: Initializes the main HTTP router for the application, applies global middleware, and registers API routes by delegating to specific handlers. It also serves static files.\n- **Definitions in the File**:\n    - **Classes / Structs / Interfaces**:\n        - `Handler`: (Public struct) Holds the `userUsecase` dependency.\n    - **Functions / Methods**:\n        - `NewHandler(userUsecase usecase.UserUsecase) *Handler`: (Public) Constructor function that creates and returns a new `Handler` instance.\n        - `(h *Handler) InitRoutes() *chi.Mux`: (Public method) Initializes a new `chi.Mux` router, applies standard middleware (Logger, Recoverer, RequestID, RealIP, Heartbeat), defines an `/api` route group for user-related endpoints, and configures serving of static files from the `./public` directory.\n- **Notable Patterns or Logic**:\n    - Centralized HTTP router setup.\n    - Uses `go-chi/chi` for routing and middleware.\n    - Middleware chain for common HTTP concerns.\n",
  "internal/transport/http/user_handler.go": "- **File Path**: `internal/transport/http/user_handler.go`\n- **High-Level Purpose**: Handles specific HTTP requests related to user operations (joining the chat, changing username) by interacting with the `UserUsecase` layer.\n- **Definitions in the File**:\n    - **Classes / Structs / Interfaces**:\n        - `UserHandler`: (Public struct) Holds the `usecase.UserUsecase` dependency.\n        - `joinRequest`: (Private struct) Data Transfer Object (DTO) for the request body of the `/join` endpoint.\n            - Fields: `DesiredUsername` (string).\n        - `joinResponse`: (Private struct) DTO for the response body of the `/join` endpoint.\n            - Fields: `UserID` (string), `Username` (string), `ActiveUsers` (interface{}).\n        - `changeUsernameRequest`: (Private struct) DTO for the request body of the `/change-username` endpoint.\n            - Fields: `UserID` (string), `NewUsername` (string).\n    - **Functions / Methods**:\n        - `NewUserHandler(uc usecase.UserUsecase) *UserHandler`: (Public) Constructor function that creates and returns a new `UserHandler` instance.\n        - `(h *UserHandler) Join(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)`: (Public method) Handles HTTP POST requests to `/api/join`. It decodes the request, calls the `UserUsecase.Join` method, and responds with the new user's details and active users, or an appropriate HTTP error status.\n        - `(h *UserHandler) ChangeUsername(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)`: (Public method) Handles HTTP POST requests to `/api/change-username`. It decodes the request, calls the `UserUsecase.ChangeUsername` method, and responds with a success status or an appropriate HTTP error status based on the usecase's error.\n- **Notable Patterns or Logic**:\n    - HTTP Handler pattern, responsible for request/response handling and delegating to the usecase layer.\n    - Uses DTOs for request and response bodies.\n    - Specific error handling and HTTP status code mapping for usecase errors.\n",
  "internal/usecase/interfaces.go": "- **File Path**: `internal/usecase/interfaces.go`\n- **High-Level Purpose**: Defines the interfaces for the `UserRepository` and `UserUsecase` components, establishing contracts for their behavior and enabling loose coupling and testability.\n- **Definitions in the File**:\n    - **Classes / Structs / Interfaces**:\n        - `UserRepository`: (Public interface) Defines the contract for data access operations related to users.\n            - Methods: `Create`, `FindByID`, `Update`, `Delete`, `GetActiveUsers`, `FindInactiveUsers`, `IsUsernameTaken`, `ReleaseUsername`, `IsUsernameOnCooldown`.\n        - `UserUsecase`: (Public interface) Defines the contract for business logic operations related to users.\n            - Methods: `Join`, `ChangeUsername`, `UpdateActivity`, `Disconnect`, `CleanupInactiveUsers`.\n- **Notable Patterns or Logic**:\n    - Interface-based programming for dependency inversion.\n",
  "internal/usecase/user_usecase.go": "- **File Path**: `internal/usecase/user_usecase.go`\n- **High-Level Purpose**: Implements the core business logic for user management, including joining, changing usernames, updating activity, disconnecting, and cleaning up inactive users. It orchestrates interactions with the `UserRepository`.\n- **Definitions in the File**:\n    - **Variables / Constants**:\n        - `ErrUsernameTaken`: (Module-level, `error`) Indicates that a desired username is already in use.\n        - `ErrUsernameOnCooldown`: (Module-level, `error`) Indicates that a desired username is currently on cooldown.\n        - `ErrUserNotFound`: (Module-level, `error`) Indicates that a user could not be found.\n        - `ErrInvalidUsername`: (Module-level, `error`) Indicates that the provided username is invalid (e.g., empty).\n    - **Classes / Structs / Interfaces**:\n        - `userUsecase`: (Private struct) Implements the `UserUsecase` interface.\n            - Fields: `userRepo` (UserRepository), `userInactiveTimeout` (time.Duration), `usernameCooldown` (time.Duration).\n    - **Functions / Methods**:\n        - `NewUserUsecase(userRepo UserRepository, inactiveTimeout, cooldown time.Duration) UserUsecase`: (Public) Constructor function that creates and returns a new `UserUsecase` instance.\n        - `(uc *userUsecase) Join(ctx context.Context, desiredUsername string) (*domain.User, []*domain.User, error)`: (Public method) Handles a user joining the chat. It trims the username, checks for availability (and appends a random number if taken), generates a new user ID, creates the user in the repository, and returns the new user and a list of active users.\n        - `(uc *userUsecase) ChangeUsername(ctx context.Context, userID, newUsername string) (string, error)`: (Public method) Allows a user to change their username. It validates the new username, checks for cooldown and availability, finds the user, updates their username, and releases the old username for cooldown.\n        - `(uc *userUsecase) UpdateActivity(ctx context.Context, userID string) error`: (Public method) Updates the `LastActive` timestamp for a given user.\n        - `(uc *userUsecase) Disconnect(ctx context.Context, userID string) (*domain.User, error)`: (Public method) Marks a user as offline in the system.\n        - `(uc *userUsecase) CleanupInactiveUsers(ctx context.Context) ([]*domain.User, error)`: (Public method) Identifies and deletes users who have been inactive for longer than the configured timeout, also releasing their usernames.\n- **Notable Patterns or Logic**:\n    - Usecase/Service layer responsible for business logic.\n    - Error handling with predefined error constants.\n    - Dependency injection of `UserRepository` and configuration durations.\n",
  "pkg/utils/idgen.go": "- **File Path**: `pkg/utils/idgen.go`\n- **High-Level Purpose**: Provides a utility function for generating universally unique identifiers (UUIDs).\n- **Definitions in the File**:\n    - **Functions / Methods**:\n        - `GenerateID()`: (Public) Returns a new unique identifier string using the `github.com/google/uuid` library.\n"
